          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
            on an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity"} infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+vector+space"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            is traditionally denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
          %p
            Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%281%29"} U(1)
            is the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+unitary+group"} projective unitary group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            be any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separably
            infinite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
          %p
          #TheTopologies.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(\mathcal{H})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operators"} bounded operators
              carries the following
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topologies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ T_k \,\in\, B(\mathcal{H}) \}_{k \in \mathbb{N}}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} converges
              to a fixed operator
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \,\in\, B(\mathcal{H})
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit
              of this sequence is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{k \to \infty}{lim} T_k \;=\; T
            %ul
              %li#NormTopology
                %p
                  …in the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm+topology"} norm topology
                  or
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology+of+uniform+convergence"} topology of uniform convergence
                  if
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi sup
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi ℋ
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mo ≤
                                %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo →
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{
                        { x \in \mathcal{H} }
                        \\atop
                        { \vert x \vert \leq 1 }
                        }{sup}
                        {\big\vert T_k(x) - T(x) \big\vert}
                        \\;\to\; 0
                        \\,;
              %li#StrongOperatorTopology
                %p
                  …in the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+operator+topology"} strong operator topology
                  or
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology+of+pointwise+convergence"} topology of pointwise convergence
                  if
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℋ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{ x \in \mathcal{H} }{\forall}  \; T_k(x) \to T(x)
                        \\,;
              %li#WeakOperatorTopology
                %p
                  …in the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+operator+topology"} weak operator topology
                  if
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℋ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{ x, y \in \mathcal{H}  }{\forall}
                        \\;
                        \\big\langle
                        T_k(x), \, y
                        \\big\rangle
                        \\to
                        \\big\langle
                        T_k(x), \, y
                        \\big\rangle
                        \\,;
              %li#CompactOpenTopology
                %p
                  …in the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
                  if
                %p
                  uniform convergence
                  %a{:href => "#NormTopology"} above
                  holds for the restrictions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_k\vert_{C}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\vert_C
                  to any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subset"} compact subset
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi ℋ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset \mathcal{H}
            %p
          (This list follows
          = succeed ".)" do
            %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014, p. 2
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
          #WithNormTopology.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a{:href => "#NormTopology"} norm topology
              makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+Lie+group"} Banach Lie group
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrizable"} metrizable
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact"} paracompact
          (For it being a Banach Lie group cf.
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"} Schottenloher 2013 p. 4/Sec. 3
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#NSW"} Nikolaus, Sachse &amp; Wockel 2013 Sec. 3
          %p
          #WithOperatorTopology.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              On
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              the
              %a{:href => "#WeakOperatorTopology"} weak operator topology
              and
              %a{:href => "#StrongOperatorTopology"} strong operator topology
              agree and make it a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
          (
          %a{:href => "#HilgertNeeb93"}> Hilgert &amp; Neeb 1993, Cor. 94
          ;
          = succeed ";" do
            %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"} Schottenloher 2013, Prop. 1
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014, Lem. 1.5
          %p
          #WithNormTopology.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a{:href => "#CompactOpenTopology"} compact-open topology
              coincides with the
              %a{:href => "#StrongOperatorTopology"} strong operator topology
          (
          %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"}> Schottenloher 2013 Prop. 2
          ;
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014, Lem. 1.8
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a{:href => "#NormTopology"} norm topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              (from Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WithNormTopology"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+topology"} operator topology
              (from Prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WithOperatorTopology"}
          (e.g.
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014, p. 5-6
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"} Schottenloher 2013, p. 4
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong summary
          #eq:DiagramOfAllTheTopologies.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi norm
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≠
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi strong
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mrow
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AA
                      %mo =
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AA
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi weak
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mrow
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AA
                      %mo =
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AA
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi comp
                      %mo .
                      %mi open
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U(\mathcal{H})_{norm}
                  \\xrightarrow{ \;\;\; \neq \;\;\; }
                  U(\mathcal{H})_{strong}
                  \\overset{ \phantom{AA} = \phantom{AA} }{\leftrightarrow}
                  U(\mathcal{H})_{weak}
                  \\overset{ \phantom{AA} = \phantom{AA} }{\leftrightarrow}
                  U(\mathcal{H})_{comp.open}
          %p
            (also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014, Thm. 1.2
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Equipped with the strong topology (Prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WithOperatorTopology"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+metric+space"} completely metrizable
          (
          %a{:href => "#Neeb97"}> Neeb 1997, Prop. II.1
          ,
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"} Schottenloher 2013 Prop. 3
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014, Lem. 1.6
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Equipped with the strong topology (Prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WithOperatorTopology"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
              is
              %em not
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
          (
          %a{:href => "#GrigorchukHarpe2014"}> Grigorchuk &amp; de la Harpe 2014, Sec. 5
          )
          %p
          #KuiperTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Kuiper’s theorem)
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H})
              in either the
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#NormTopology"} norm topology
            %p or the
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#StrongOperatorTopology"} strong operator topology
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#WeakOperatorTopology"} weak operator topology
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#CompactOpenTopology"} compact-open topology
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              in that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \;\colon\; U(\mathcal{H}) \to U(\mathcal{H})
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi const
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const_{\mathrm{e}} \;\colon\; U(\mathcal{H}) \to U(\mathcal{H})
          See the
          %a{:href => "Kuiper's+theorem#References"} references
          at
          = succeed "." do
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuiper%27s+theorem"} Kuiper's theorem
          %p
          #UHCircleFiberBundle.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%281%29"} U(1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} coprojection
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"} U(ℋ)
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
              – both in their strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+topology"} operator topology
              – is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi PU
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ≃
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℋ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^1 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H})
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; PU(\mathcal{H})
                    \\mathrlap{ \; \simeq \; \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H})/S^1 }
                    }
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "#Simms70"}> Simms 1970, Thm. 1
          )
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UHCircleFiberBundle"}
              means in particular that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H}) \xrightarrow{\;} PU(\mathcal{H})
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial+bundle"} locally trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} coprojection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H}) \xrightarrow{\;} \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H})/S^1
              admits
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+sections"} local sections
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space+coprojection+admitting+local+sections"} coset space coprojection admitting local sections
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+unitary+group"} stable unitary group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-parameter+semigroup"} one-parameter semigroup
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+equivariant+PU%28%E2%84%8B%29-bundle"} universal equivariant PU(ℋ)-bundle
          %h2#References References
          %p
            Early discussion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathscr{H})
            motivated from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            and in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
          %ul
            %li#Simms68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+John+Simms"}> David John Simms
                , pp. 5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie Groups and Quantum Mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 52
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0069914"} doi:10.1007/BFb0069914
            %li#Simms70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+John+Simms"}> David John Simms
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological aspects of the projective unitary group
                %strong 68
                1 (1970) 57-60 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100001043"}> doi:10.1017/S0305004100001043
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p#SimmsFalseClaim
            Beware of the false claim in
            %a{:href => "#Simms68"} Simms 1968 p. 10
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"} U(ℋ)
            is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+operator+topology"} strong operator topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"} Schottenloher 2013
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#EspinozaUribe14"} Espinoza &amp; Uribe 2014
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schottenloher95"} Schottenloher 1995
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahSegal04"} Atiyah &amp; Segal 2004
          %p
            The mistake arises because multiplication in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(\mathscr{H})
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+operators"}> bounded linear operators
            ) is not generally continuous in the strong operator topology, according to
          %ul
            %li#Naimark59
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Naimark"} Mark Naimark
              (translated by Leo Boron), §33.2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Normed Rings
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/normedrings0000mana"} ark:/13960/s20rdczxmrt
          %p
            whence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathscr{H})
            is indeed not a topological group in the strong operator topology, which however does not imply that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathscr{H}) \subset GL(\mathscr{H})
            cannot have that property (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Schottenloher13"} Schottenloher 2013 p 2-3
          %p
            Proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
            is a topological group in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+operator+topology"} strong operator topology
          %ul
            %li#Schottenloher95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"}> Martin Schottenloher
                , Thm. 3.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometrie und Symmetrie in der Physik – Leitmotiv der Mathematischen Physik
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-322-89928-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-322-89928-6
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~schotten/bas/Geometrie%20und%20Symmetrie.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Schottenloher08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"}> Martin Schottenloher
                , Prop. 3.11 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Mathematical Introduction to Conformal Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 759
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-540-68628-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-68628-6
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~schotten/LNP-cft-pdf/"} web
          %p
            Proof that the weak- and strong-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+topologies"} operator topologies
            agree on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
          %ul
            %li#HilgertNeeb93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Hilgert"}> Joachim Hilgert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karl-Hermann+Neeb"} Karl-Hermann Neeb
              = succeed "." do
                %em Lie Semigroups and their Applications
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1552
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0084640"} doi:10.1007/BFb0084640
          %p
            Proof that weak-, strong- as well as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
            all agree on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
          %ul
            %li#Schottenloher13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"}> Martin Schottenloher
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Unitary Group In Its Strong Topology
                %strong 08
                05 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.scirp.org/html/4-5301487_84967.htm"}> doi:10.4236/apm.2018.85029
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.5891"} arXiv:1309.5891
            %li#EspinozaUribe14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesus+Espinoza"}> Jesus Espinoza
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"} Bernardo Uribe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological properties of the unitary group
                %strong 16
                1 (2014) 45-55 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1407.1869"}> arXiv:1407.1869
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.pphmj.com/abstract/8730.htm"} journal
          %p
            Previous influential but wrong claim that they do not and that the compact open topology does not even make a topological group (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SimmsFalseClaim"} above
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Simms68"} Simms 1968 p 10
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahSegal04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twisted K-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0407054"} arXiv:math/0407054
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://iamm.su/en/journals/j879/?VID=10"} journal page
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://iamm.su/upload/iblock/45e/t1-n3-287-330.pdf"} published pdf
          %p Further properties:
          %p Proof of complete metrizability for the strong (and hence weak) operator topology:
          %ul
            %li#Neeb97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karl-Hermann+Neeb"}> Karl-Hermann Neeb
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On a Theorem of S. Banach
              %strong 8
              (1997) 293–300 (
              %a{:href => "https://www.heldermann-verlag.de/jlt/jlt07/NEEBPL.PDF"}> pdf
              )
          %p Proof of failure of local compactness:
          %ul
            %li#GrigorchukHarpe2014
              Rostislav Grigorchuk, Pierre de la Harpe,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Amenability and ergodic properties of topological groups: from Bogolyubov onwards
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groups, Graphs and Random Walks
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.7030"} arXiv:1404.7030
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316576571.011"} doi:10.1017/9781316576571.011
          %p
            Proof of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazhdan%27s+property+%28T%29"} Kazhdan's property (T)
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathcal{H})
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bachir+Bekka"}> Bachir Bekka
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kazhdan’s Property (T) for the unitary group of a separable Hilbert space
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00039-003-0420-0"} doi:10.1007/s00039-003-0420-0
            %li#NSW
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Sachse"} Christoph Sachse
                = succeed "," do
